<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Coverage collection settings for the backend suites. Driven by the two commands recorded in
  backend/tools/check-coverage.cs (a runsettings file cannot quote them: an XML comment may not
  contain a double hyphen).

  DELIBERATELY MINIMAL. It configures WHAT is instrumented (the four product assemblies, never the
  test assemblies) and the report format, and nothing else.

  In particular it does NOT use coverlet's ExcludeByFile to drop the generated EF migrations from the
  denominator, even though that is the obvious place for it, for two reasons:

    1. ExcludeByFile is a GLOB, and a glob is exactly how the client's coverage gate went wrong in
       P3a: whether `*` crosses `/` differs between tools and versions, the pattern silently
       under-excluded nested generated files, and the gate reported 58.6% against a true 97.60%. The
       exclusion therefore lives in check-coverage.cs as an ordinal PATH match, where it is
       deterministic and testable. Same reasoning, same shape, as client/tool/check_coverage.dart.

    2. Excluding at COLLECTION time destroys the whole-tree number. G15 requires BOTH figures to be
       reported: the hand-written one the 70% exit criterion is measured against, and the whole-tree
       one that keeps nobody from mistaking 95% for whole-tree coverage. A partitioning checker
       reports both from one run; an ExcludeByFile run can only ever report one.

  No filters beyond the assembly Include/Exclude, so the denominator stays comparable with the T9
  measurement G15 quotes (SkipAutoProps and friends would silently move the number).
-->
<RunSettings>
  <DataCollectionRunSettings>
    <DataCollectors>
      <DataCollector friendlyName="XPlat code coverage">
        <Configuration>
          <Format>cobertura</Format>
          <Include>[Lumen.Api]*,[Lumen.Application]*,[Lumen.Domain]*,[Lumen.Infrastructure]*</Include>
          <Exclude>[Lumen.UnitTests]*,[Lumen.IntegrationTests]*,[Lumen.SecurityTests]*</Exclude>
          <UseSourceLink>false</UseSourceLink>
        </Configuration>
      </DataCollector>
    </DataCollectors>
  </DataCollectionRunSettings>
</RunSettings>
